      "message": "This file mostly follows android\u0027s pandora server implementation.\nhost interface from android:\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Bluetooth/android/pandora/server/src/Host.kt?q\u003dhost.kt\n\nFor us now the only user is PTS-bot. PTS-bot use mmi2grpc interface to call the\nBLuetooth test server.\nmmi2grpc:\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/android/pandora/mmi2grpc/mmi2grpc/\n\nmore info for PTS-bot:\nhttps://docs.google.com/document/d/1TDRiiCpetikQIAP13J8uT_eXGwcpFnclyav_z5J3OUo/edit?resourcekey\u003d0-uUqq2xn_KfsVvW_6apo_9A#heading\u003dh.ljddzha3fj7\n\nThe original interface descriptions in https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:external/pandora/bt-test-interfaces/pandora/host.proto?q\u003dhost.proto may be not clear enough so I decide\nto align with android if anything is not clear.\n\nFor example:\n\"Manufacturer Specific Data\" in advertising data type is composed with:\n\n Company Identifier Code | manufacturer specific data.\n \nIn android\u0027s implementation, manufacturer_data is the second part of the \"Manufacturer Specific Data\" according to: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Bluetooth/android/pandora/server/src/Host.kt;l\u003d562?q\u003dhost.kt. And this is unclear\nif we only look at the proto file. May be the better way is to discuss with android team to improve the proto definition in the future.",
